		(property "Note" "12V pass-through to the X1202 UPS. REV 2.0 moved this from +12V_RAW to +12V, i.e. downstream of Q1 and D1, so the Pi's supply is now behind both reverse-polarity and transient protection for the first time. Costs no headroom: Q1 drops 38 mV at the 3A budget where a series Schottky would have dropped ~500 mV, which is why the tap was originally moved upstream."
			(at 0 0 0)
			(hide yes)
