		(property "Quote" "Not yet quoted - added rev 2.0. Verified in distributor stock 2026-08-23."
			(at 0 0 0)
			(hide yes)
			(show_name no)
			(do_not_autoplace no)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1.27 1.27)
				)
				(justify left)
			)
		)
		(property "Note" "12V sense divider, high side. 100k/22k gives ratio 0.1803: 14.4V -> 2.60V, 16V -> 2.89V. NOT the Macchina M2's 10.0k/2.20k - same ratio, ten times the impedance. This divider cannot be switched off (the rev 3.0 supervisor needs it live to decide when to wake), and at 10k it would draw ~1.18 mA, consuming S13.3.1's entire <1 mA sleep budget alone. At 100k it draws 118 uA. The 100k also removes the need for a clamp diode: with the ADC's own input protection holding the node at 3.6V, fault current at D1's 38.9V clamp is (38.9-3.6)/100k = 353 uA against TI's +/-10 mA continuous input rating."
			(at 0 0 0)
			(hide yes)
			(show_name no)
			(do_not_autoplace no)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1.27 1.27)
				)
				(justify left)
			)
		)
