		(property "Note" "ADS1015 input charge reservoir and anti-alias filter. Against the divider's 18.0k Thevenin source impedance, 10n puts the corner at ~880 Hz - high enough to pass alternator ripple and crank transients (which S13.3.3b wants from this same divider at kHz rates in rev 3.0), low enough to reject switching noise and RF. DO NOT raise to 100n without re-reading that section: it would give a quieter DC reading at ~88 Hz but destroy the crank-profiling ambition. Average in software instead if the reading is noisy."
			(at 0 0 0)
			(hide yes)
