		(property "Note" "Vehicle harness terminal block. PINS 4-6 WERE RE-ASSIGNED IN REV 2.0 for cleaner routing - pin 4 is now CAN High, pin 5 CAN Low, pin 6 K-line (previously K-line, CAN High, CAN Low). A HARNESS BUILT TO THE REV 1.0 PINOUT WILL PUT CAN HIGH ON THE K-LINE PIN. Pins 1 = +12V (OBD 16), 2 = signal ground (OBD 5), 3 = chassis ground (OBD 4), 4 = CANH (OBD 6), 5 = CANL (OBD 14), 6 = K-line (OBD 7). Pins 2 and 3 are the same GND net, so this board is the bonding point between the two returns - join them at a single star point near the connector. For bench work, clamp 120 ohm across pins 4 and 5; the board carries no CAN termination by design."
			(at 0 0 0)
			(hide yes)
			(show_name no)
			(do_not_autoplace no)
