					(size 1.27 1.27)
				)
				(justify left)
			)
		)
		(property "Note" "REV 2.0: reverse-polarity protection for the whole board, replacing D4 (SS54), which was removed as redundant. ORIENTATION IS A SILENT FAILURE MODE: drain (pad 2, the tab) faces the input +12V_RAW; source (pad 3) faces +12V. The body diode must conduct input->output. Reversed, the board powers up and runs normally and the defect only appears the day J2 is miswired - which is the only day it matters. Verify on a current-limited bench supply before the board goes in the vehicle: correct polarity shows a near-zero drop across Q1, reversed draws nothing. Rds(on) 15 mOhm at Vgs=-10V gives 38 mV and 0.11W at the 3A budget, against the SS54 it replaces at ~500 mV and ~1.5W - which is the whole point, since S3.7.4 moved the Pi tap upstream precisely to keep a diode drop out of a supply that must survive cranking sag. -60V clears D1 SMBJ24A max clamping voltage of 38.9V. CONFIRM Vgs(max) FROM THE PART DATASHEET before ordering - the selection guide does not list it and D3 was sized assuming the usual +/-20V."
			(at 0 0 0)
			(hide yes)
			(show_name no)
			(do_not_autoplace no)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1.27 1.27)
				)
				(justify left)
			)
		)
		(property "Quote" "MPN set to the Vishay base part number, consistent with this board's treatment of SS54 and 1N4148W. Packaging/RoHS suffix (-E3 / -GE3 style) is a distributor choice at order time."
			(at 0 0 0)
			(hide yes)
			(show_name no)
